    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR) to owner creation and returns a derived `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nSince this project is judged black-box (POST creates, GET reads back), `title` has to persist. I made these changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (optional, enum MR/MRS/MS/DR) to the `OwnerFields` request schema, and `salutation` (readOnly) to the `Owner` response schema. The DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`) are generated from this at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added a `title` column with getter/setter so it persists and flows through the pipeline.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `salutation` MapStruct mapping:\n   `title == null/blank ? lastName : title + \" \" + lastName`. The `title` field itself maps automatically by name (request DTO \u2192 entity \u2192 response DTO).\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in schema.sql.\n\nNo new OfficeFloor function classes were needed \u2014 the existing `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2192 `BuildOwner` \u2192 \u2026 \u2192 `RespondWithOwner` pipeline carries the new field through the mapper unchanged. The new `coreComposesSalutation` acceptance test passes (`GET` returns `salutation` = `\"DR who\"`), and the full suite is green.",
